+## 10. Individual due-date extension — `mod_assign_save_user_extensions`
+
+Resolve the assignment instance ID from the current course binding and the student's user
+ID by matching email in `mod_assign_list_participants`. Preview that exact recipient and
+assignment with the new local date and time, and obtain approval under the common write
+protocol. Never change the assignment-wide due date to grant one student's exception.
+
+```text
+wsfunction=mod_assign_save_user_extensions
+assignmentid=<assignment-instance-id>
+userids[0]=<user-id>
+dates[0]=<Unix timestamp of the new due date>
+```
+
+Send this through the binding's Python POST transport with credentials read privately, not
+through `lms_read.py` (which remains read-only). Success returns an empty list; prove the
+result with `mod_assign_get_submission_status` and compare
+`lastattempt.extensionduedate` to the intended timestamp. Stop on an API error or mismatch.
+
+If the instructor supplies only a date, use the course's usual deadline time from
+`lms/course.yaml` and state the assumed time in the preview. Resolve the timezone from that
+course policy; for these NC State offerings it is `America/New_York`. Build the timestamp
+with an aware `datetime` and `zoneinfo.ZoneInfo`, never a naive local datetime. Keep the
+assignment, recipient, expected timestamp and read-back result in the nonsecret operations
+audit. No grading sheet or grade write is needed for this operation.
